1
00:01:02,229 --> 00:01:04,690
The bullet nicked
the artery near his collarbone,

2
00:01:04,774 --> 00:01:06,859
but it luckily missed his nerve cord.

3
00:01:07,443 --> 00:01:08,819
The surgery went well.

4
00:01:09,236 --> 00:01:12,031
He should regain consciousness
by today, sir.

5
00:01:22,666 --> 00:01:25,920
Managing Director Yoon asked me
to come to you if something happens.

6
00:01:26,337 --> 00:01:29,048
He said you were the only one
who could stop Ms. Yoon Mi-jin.

7
00:01:29,131 --> 00:01:29,965
But before that,

8
00:01:32,676 --> 00:01:34,345
I also have something to tell you.

9
00:01:40,267 --> 00:01:41,393
No!

10
00:01:41,477 --> 00:01:43,062
If it weren't for Detective Kang,

11
00:01:43,604 --> 00:01:45,314
he wouldn't have stood a chance.

12
00:01:50,194 --> 00:01:52,446
If the other detectives
came a second too late,

13
00:01:54,448 --> 00:01:56,075
-that also
-Where's backup?

14
00:01:56,158 --> 00:01:58,202
would've led to the worst-case scenario.

15
00:01:58,536 --> 00:01:59,745
Take him over there!

16
00:02:35,489 --> 00:02:36,532
Jae-hee.

17
00:02:40,828 --> 00:02:41,745
Jae-hee!

18
00:02:51,338 --> 00:02:52,548
We managed to save her,

19
00:02:53,007 --> 00:02:54,842
but we'll have to keep monitoring her.

20
00:03:03,976 --> 00:03:04,894
What did he say?

21
00:03:06,645 --> 00:03:07,855
She's in hypovolemic shock

22
00:03:08,731 --> 00:03:10,149
due to severe hemorrhage.

23
00:03:10,858 --> 00:03:14,069
If she doesn't regain consciousness,
I won't just stand back.

24
00:03:14,612 --> 00:03:15,529
Damn it.

25
00:03:16,196 --> 00:03:17,448
Let's get Yoon Mi-jin.

26
00:03:18,574 --> 00:03:19,867
We need to get something.

27
00:03:22,161 --> 00:03:24,455
-Where's Jae-hee?
-Jae-hee!

28
00:03:24,538 --> 00:03:25,873
-Jae-hee!
-Where is she?

29
00:03:25,956 --> 00:03:27,207
-Where's Jae-hee?
-Tell me.

30
00:03:27,291 --> 00:03:29,084
-My daughter.
-Jae-hee.

31
00:03:29,168 --> 00:03:31,879
No! Jae-hee!

32
00:03:32,254 --> 00:03:34,423
Jae-hee!

33
00:03:35,174 --> 00:03:37,635
I heard he's not going to
last much longer.

34
00:03:37,718 --> 00:03:39,261
Didn't you see the news?

35
00:03:39,470 --> 00:03:42,723
"Third-generation of T Group
in a coma at the ER."

36
00:03:43,641 --> 00:03:44,975
I heard he's on a ventilator.

37
00:03:45,476 --> 00:03:48,354
I thought he was going to Taekang Retail.
This is so unfortunate.

38
00:03:48,812 --> 00:03:51,231
I heard he was the one
who embezzled the slush fund.

39
00:03:51,315 --> 00:03:53,150
What's that about?

40
00:03:54,485 --> 00:03:56,612
-Honey.
-I already read it.

41
00:03:58,781 --> 00:04:01,033
We never have a moment of peace
because of Yi-jun.

42
00:04:01,825 --> 00:04:04,745
They say he can hear everything
even while he's unconscious.

43
00:04:04,828 --> 00:04:06,330
Wouldn't hearing our voices

44
00:04:06,664 --> 00:04:08,082
give Yi-jun some strength?

45
00:04:08,791 --> 00:04:10,084
Please let us see him.

46
00:04:10,960 --> 00:04:14,004
Forget visiting him.
That's not the priority right now.

47
00:04:14,755 --> 00:04:16,423
What about the shareholder meeting?

48
00:04:18,509 --> 00:04:19,718
Shouldn't we postpone it?

49
00:04:20,219 --> 00:04:22,346
Sir, information
keeps leaking to the press.

50
00:04:22,429 --> 00:04:25,140
-It'd be better to--
-Call a board meeting.

51
00:04:25,891 --> 00:04:27,142
Contain the chaos first.

52
00:04:28,352 --> 00:04:29,812
Are you pushing back the meeting?

53
00:04:31,230 --> 00:04:32,231
Or…

54
00:04:33,232 --> 00:04:35,401
are you going to change the CEO candidate?

55
00:05:09,727 --> 00:05:12,229
Officially, you haven't regained
consciousness yet.

56
00:05:12,312 --> 00:05:14,732
You made that call. What's with you?

57
00:05:16,191 --> 00:05:17,943
Jae-hee is not waking up.

58
00:05:21,196 --> 00:05:22,031
Yi-jun.

59
00:05:22,114 --> 00:05:24,199
I'm really sorry I couldn't hold her back.

60
00:05:24,283 --> 00:05:26,660
But you need to pull yourself together.

61
00:05:26,744 --> 00:05:28,287
Let's get you back to your room.

62
00:05:30,039 --> 00:05:31,415
She's not opening her eyes.

63
00:05:39,798 --> 00:05:40,924
Chairman Yoon is here.

64
00:05:46,055 --> 00:05:47,765
I called a board meeting.

65
00:05:47,848 --> 00:05:51,226
It looks like Mi-jin
might get reappointed.

66
00:05:52,936 --> 00:05:55,939
Many people were sacrificed
because of Mi-jin's ruthless greed.

67
00:05:56,440 --> 00:05:58,275
She has to be stopped

68
00:05:58,984 --> 00:06:00,444
before she sacrifices even more.

69
00:06:02,488 --> 00:06:03,447
That's why

70
00:06:04,239 --> 00:06:05,616
I did as you asked.

71
00:06:05,699 --> 00:06:08,452
Didn't I play along
with your pathetic little act?

72
00:06:09,453 --> 00:06:11,830
My patience ends here with cowards

73
00:06:12,581 --> 00:06:13,582
who plot in secret.

74
00:06:14,625 --> 00:06:15,542
Sir.

75
00:06:16,043 --> 00:06:20,589
I understand you want hard data
on the damage Ms. Yoon did to the company

76
00:06:20,672 --> 00:06:21,673
before you can act.

77
00:06:21,757 --> 00:06:23,342
-But the situation--
-Exactly.

78
00:06:25,385 --> 00:06:28,514
How I deal with Mi-jin
is up to what you do,

79
00:06:29,306 --> 00:06:30,349
not what you say.

80
00:06:37,481 --> 00:06:38,565
Bring me proof.

81
00:06:52,621 --> 00:06:55,749
We can't win the board meeting by a vote.

82
00:06:55,833 --> 00:06:58,210
Right now, I don't care what happens.

83
00:06:59,002 --> 00:07:02,297
More importantly,
I was too cruel to Jae-hee.

84
00:07:04,091 --> 00:07:06,552
I shouldn't have said
things I didn't mean.

85
00:07:09,346 --> 00:07:10,973
I regret that the most.

86
00:07:33,495 --> 00:07:34,329
Mom.

87
00:07:35,956 --> 00:07:38,041
-Mom.
-Honey.

88
00:07:39,710 --> 00:07:41,712
-She's up. Jae-hee!
-Jae-hee!

89
00:07:41,920 --> 00:07:42,838
That hurts.

90
00:07:43,255 --> 00:07:44,756
-You're awake.
-Are you okay?

91
00:07:46,967 --> 00:07:47,801
I'm okay.

92
00:07:47,885 --> 00:07:50,554
-Thank goodness.
-Thank goodness.

93
00:07:50,637 --> 00:07:53,765
I'm so grateful you're back, sweetheart.

94
00:07:57,561 --> 00:07:58,478
What?

95
00:08:00,189 --> 00:08:01,315
Yoon Yi-jun.

96
00:08:01,982 --> 00:08:02,941
Goodness.

97
00:08:05,986 --> 00:08:07,321
What about him?

98
00:08:08,155 --> 00:08:09,990
-Goodness.
-Is he okay?

99
00:08:10,365 --> 00:08:12,242
Yes, he's okay.

100
00:08:12,826 --> 00:08:14,494
He's fine.

101
00:08:24,171 --> 00:08:25,339
I can't believe you two.

102
00:08:37,935 --> 00:08:39,144
You can go in.

103
00:08:59,915 --> 00:09:00,832
Thank you,

104
00:09:02,000 --> 00:09:02,918
Jae-hee.

105
00:09:03,710 --> 00:09:05,003
I'm glad.

106
00:09:08,215 --> 00:09:10,050
I'm glad you're okay.

107
00:09:23,981 --> 00:09:26,483
FINAL EPISODE

108
00:09:29,361 --> 00:09:31,488
The time has come to make a decision

109
00:09:32,155 --> 00:09:34,157
for the future of Taekang Retail.

110
00:09:34,241 --> 00:09:38,412
We will revoke the previous resolution
naming Managing Director Yoon Yi-jun

111
00:09:39,121 --> 00:09:40,247
as the next CEO.

112
00:09:41,290 --> 00:09:43,250
Will the chairman be attending?

113
00:09:43,750 --> 00:09:45,794
Father called the board meeting himself.

114
00:09:47,296 --> 00:09:50,674
It's heartbreaking to think about
my brother who is fighting for his life,

115
00:09:50,757 --> 00:09:53,635
but I will honor my father's wishes

116
00:09:54,344 --> 00:09:58,473
and minimize disruption to the company
during this crisis.

117
00:09:58,682 --> 00:10:00,600
If we revoke the previous resolution

118
00:10:00,684 --> 00:10:04,396
and immediately reappoint Ms. Yoon Mi-jin,

119
00:10:04,896 --> 00:10:06,815
we won't need to hold
a shareholder meeting.

120
00:10:07,649 --> 00:10:09,985
This is within
our board's authority, isn't it?

121
00:10:11,570 --> 00:10:13,196
If you cooperate,

122
00:10:13,739 --> 00:10:16,408
I will reward you accordingly.

123
00:10:19,328 --> 00:10:21,246
I told you I'd find it, didn't I?

124
00:10:22,914 --> 00:10:26,335
Confess before you
take the fall for everyone.

125
00:10:26,418 --> 00:10:29,254
There's this thing called a base station,
you idiot.

126
00:10:29,463 --> 00:10:32,215
There's one in Seohui-dong,
where Yoon Mi-jin lives.

127
00:10:41,725 --> 00:10:42,893
Rings a bell, doesn't it?

128
00:10:47,314 --> 00:10:49,900
-Yes?
-Hey, Jae-hee woke up.

129
00:10:50,400 --> 00:10:51,276
Really?

130
00:10:58,408 --> 00:11:00,369
Why? You want to drink some water?

131
00:11:01,286 --> 00:11:02,454
Stay put.

132
00:11:03,997 --> 00:11:06,333
Here. Drink slowly.

133
00:11:08,418 --> 00:11:09,419
Is that enough?

134
00:11:14,216 --> 00:11:15,133
What is it?

135
00:11:15,926 --> 00:11:16,760
Does it hurt a lot?

136
00:11:18,261 --> 00:11:19,846
Why did you get in front of me?

137
00:11:22,307 --> 00:11:25,936
Why did you take a bullet for me?
You could've gotten seriously injured.

138
00:11:27,479 --> 00:11:30,148
Then, what about you?

139
00:11:30,232 --> 00:11:31,775
You and I are different.

140
00:11:31,858 --> 00:11:33,527
I'm trained.

141
00:11:33,610 --> 00:11:36,738
I had no time to think about that
because you were in danger.

142
00:11:38,240 --> 00:11:39,533
I didn't care about myself.

143
00:11:39,616 --> 00:11:42,160
I was worried about keeping you safe.

144
00:11:42,244 --> 00:11:44,704
How could you be so irresponsible?

145
00:11:45,038 --> 00:11:46,081
Then what about me?

146
00:11:46,581 --> 00:11:49,334
You may not care
about what happens to you,

147
00:11:49,668 --> 00:11:51,211
but I would be left all alone.

148
00:11:51,670 --> 00:11:53,672
Then you're just as irresponsible.

149
00:11:53,755 --> 00:11:55,757
These past few days, I just thought,

150
00:11:55,841 --> 00:11:57,676
"What if I have to live alone forever?"

151
00:11:57,759 --> 00:12:00,345
"If she dies, should I just follow her?"

152
00:12:00,429 --> 00:12:02,097
-Yi-jun!
-Take it easy.

153
00:12:02,180 --> 00:12:04,015
Don't yell.

154
00:12:04,099 --> 00:12:05,350
What if your stitches burst?

155
00:12:05,434 --> 00:12:09,104
He keeps coming here every day
instead of staying in his own room.

156
00:12:09,187 --> 00:12:11,189
He must be thrilled
out of his mind by now.

157
00:12:11,273 --> 00:12:13,900
We're happy she's safe.
Imagine how he must feel.

158
00:12:13,984 --> 00:12:14,985
Here.

159
00:12:15,318 --> 00:12:16,194
Wait.

160
00:12:16,862 --> 00:12:18,488
Should we knock first?

161
00:12:19,072 --> 00:12:21,867
They must be so emotional
from being reunited,

162
00:12:21,950 --> 00:12:24,995
they might've forgotten
they're in a hospital or something.

163
00:12:25,078 --> 00:12:26,997
-Jeez, just move.
-I saved you for a reason!

164
00:12:27,497 --> 00:12:29,958
-What's the point of life without you?
-They're fighting.

165
00:12:30,041 --> 00:12:33,628
No matter what danger comes our way,
I'll protect you from now on.

166
00:12:33,712 --> 00:12:35,297
Then hold my hand!

167
00:12:38,467 --> 00:12:39,593
Or hug me.

168
00:12:39,676 --> 00:12:40,677
I was going to.

169
00:12:41,720 --> 00:12:43,263
They're not fighting.

170
00:12:43,346 --> 00:12:45,640
They're just being
sickly sweet to each other.

171
00:12:45,724 --> 00:12:47,350
Should we wait?

172
00:12:47,434 --> 00:12:48,935
-I don't think we should--
-Hey!

173
00:12:49,019 --> 00:12:50,103
-Get back here!
-Hey!

174
00:12:53,940 --> 00:12:57,235
You two were fighting just now, right?
You weren't doing anything funny?

175
00:12:57,319 --> 00:12:58,445
Did you hear us?

176
00:12:58,528 --> 00:13:00,071
Is it okay if we come in?

177
00:13:00,614 --> 00:13:02,824
Good grief. You little brat.

178
00:13:02,908 --> 00:13:04,493
I can't believe you.

179
00:13:04,576 --> 00:13:06,745
-Is it this side or this side?
-Don't touch it.

180
00:13:06,828 --> 00:13:08,288
This is unlike you. Get up.

181
00:13:11,374 --> 00:13:12,501
She's still a patient.

182
00:13:19,174 --> 00:13:22,177
No one wanted you
to recover more than I did.

183
00:13:23,053 --> 00:13:25,931
I got so scared
when you told me to move last time.

184
00:13:26,389 --> 00:13:27,766
I'm glad that you're better.

185
00:13:28,850 --> 00:13:29,935
Right.

186
00:13:30,018 --> 00:13:32,729
But things did get a bit complicated.

187
00:13:37,275 --> 00:13:40,403
I guess it's almost over.

188
00:13:47,160 --> 00:13:50,080
2026 TAEKANG RETAIL
EXTRAORDINARY BOARD MEETING

189
00:13:50,163 --> 00:13:52,082
CHAIRMAN YOON TAE-SIK

190
00:13:52,165 --> 00:13:53,542
CEO YOON MI-JIN

191
00:14:05,845 --> 00:14:06,763
Good luck, ma'am.

192
00:14:12,644 --> 00:14:13,979
NA-JUNG

193
00:14:43,258 --> 00:14:44,092
Mi-jin.

194
00:14:48,388 --> 00:14:49,264
See?

195
00:14:49,598 --> 00:14:50,849
She didn't know either.

196
00:14:51,474 --> 00:14:53,810
Can you believe he awakened
right before the meeting?

197
00:14:57,272 --> 00:14:59,608
I'll call this extraordinary board meeting
to order

198
00:14:59,691 --> 00:15:01,318
due to the nominee's injury.

199
00:15:06,281 --> 00:15:09,075
I am the CEO of Taekang Retail,
Yoon Mi-jin.

200
00:15:09,159 --> 00:15:10,702
The first agenda is

201
00:15:10,785 --> 00:15:14,080
the withdrawal of
Yoon Yi-jun's nomination as CEO.

202
00:15:14,873 --> 00:15:17,459
Next, we'll hold a vote by show of hands

203
00:15:17,834 --> 00:15:19,669
on whether to reappoint the current CEO.

204
00:15:23,381 --> 00:15:26,134
Yoon Yi-jun's support among the staff
is at an all-time low.

205
00:15:26,426 --> 00:15:28,011
He'll never turn this around.

206
00:15:30,513 --> 00:15:32,557
We will begin with the vote

207
00:15:32,641 --> 00:15:34,517
to revoke the CEO nomination.

208
00:15:35,143 --> 00:15:37,228
Those in favor, please raise your hands.

209
00:15:54,204 --> 00:15:55,580
Five in favor.

210
00:15:58,541 --> 00:15:59,584
Six in favor.

211
00:16:03,755 --> 00:16:05,215
Are there any others in favor?

212
00:16:06,591 --> 00:16:08,051
You had no other cards to play.

213
00:16:19,104 --> 00:16:20,313
Hold on.

214
00:16:30,031 --> 00:16:31,282
I'm not in favor,

215
00:16:31,366 --> 00:16:33,827
but I was wondering
if I may have the floor.

216
00:16:41,376 --> 00:16:42,210
You may.

217
00:16:43,294 --> 00:16:46,631
I just got a video you might all enjoy.

218
00:16:49,217 --> 00:16:51,344
It'd be a shame to watch it alone.

219
00:16:57,559 --> 00:17:00,061
Before I show this,
I'd like to ask you a question.

220
00:17:00,603 --> 00:17:03,481
Have any of you ever been shot?

221
00:17:08,486 --> 00:17:09,696
No one?

222
00:17:11,072 --> 00:17:12,240
I've been shot.

223
00:17:14,743 --> 00:17:16,035
Do you know how it feels?

224
00:17:21,207 --> 00:17:22,167
It hurts.

225
00:17:23,668 --> 00:17:26,546
All I did was
look for Taekang's slush fund,

226
00:17:26,629 --> 00:17:27,881
but why

227
00:17:29,466 --> 00:17:30,675
did someone shoot me?

228
00:17:30,759 --> 00:17:32,302
I'm very curious.

229
00:17:35,388 --> 00:17:36,598
That's why…

230
00:17:36,681 --> 00:17:39,184
This is irrelevant to the board--

231
00:17:39,267 --> 00:17:40,727
My apologies.

232
00:17:40,810 --> 00:17:42,395
MANAGING DIRECTOR YOON YI-JUN

233
00:17:44,272 --> 00:17:47,734
I was supposed to show you this first,
but I forgot about it.

234
00:17:51,946 --> 00:17:52,989
Manager Park!

235
00:18:04,709 --> 00:18:07,045
TOTAL AMOUNT EMBEZZLED:
501,914,400,000 WON

236
00:18:13,468 --> 00:18:14,677
As you can see,

237
00:18:15,094 --> 00:18:17,055
these are abnormal fund flows.

238
00:18:17,931 --> 00:18:21,559
Hundreds of billions of won were funneled
to companies in tax havens.

239
00:18:22,310 --> 00:18:23,686
Forensic accounting

240
00:18:23,770 --> 00:18:27,148
has verified these
as genuine transaction records.

241
00:18:28,233 --> 00:18:31,402
This is crazy.
What the hell are you even talking about?

242
00:18:31,486 --> 00:18:34,447
Ultimately, we identified that

243
00:18:35,824 --> 00:18:38,910
CEO Yoon Mi-jin was responsible
for this operation.

244
00:18:43,498 --> 00:18:44,582
This has been forged.

245
00:18:44,833 --> 00:18:46,626
Someone fabricated them to frame me!

246
00:18:46,709 --> 00:18:47,710
Directors.

247
00:18:48,211 --> 00:18:49,462
Let's watch this next.

248
00:18:49,546 --> 00:18:50,839
I learned this from Father.

249
00:18:50,922 --> 00:18:52,382
If you cooperate,

250
00:18:52,966 --> 00:18:55,301
I will reward you accordingly.

251
00:18:56,970 --> 00:18:58,638
Excuse me. I have a question.

252
00:18:58,721 --> 00:19:00,056
Sorry, just a second.

253
00:19:00,139 --> 00:19:02,684
The lights are so dim.
Could you come this way?

254
00:19:03,351 --> 00:19:05,311
Could you recommend something affordable?

255
00:19:05,395 --> 00:19:07,355
We have the lunch special.

256
00:19:07,438 --> 00:19:08,815
This one? Does it include stew?

257
00:19:08,898 --> 00:19:10,525
Yes. A spicy stew is included…

258
00:19:13,903 --> 00:19:16,823
The board meeting day, 11 a.m.
Shopping mall in Gari-dong.

259
00:19:16,906 --> 00:19:18,283
She promised the directors

260
00:19:18,366 --> 00:19:20,869
to give them cash and bonds.

261
00:19:21,202 --> 00:19:22,954
We got a statement from the sniper.

262
00:19:23,413 --> 00:19:26,291
We traced the gun's source
and matched the payment records.

263
00:19:27,625 --> 00:19:29,752
It was from
one of Yoon Mi-jin's fake accounts.

264
00:19:29,836 --> 00:19:30,920
Get everyone!

265
00:19:31,004 --> 00:19:32,297
-Get him!
-Shit.

266
00:19:32,380 --> 00:19:33,590
Hey, he's getting away.

267
00:19:33,673 --> 00:19:34,716
Get back here!

268
00:19:46,644 --> 00:19:48,229
Jae-hee! Is your arm okay?

269
00:19:48,313 --> 00:19:51,649
A little scratch on my arm is nothing
when you're out here working.

270
00:19:51,733 --> 00:19:55,153
Mr. Yoon is going to lose it
if he finds out you came here.

271
00:19:56,112 --> 00:19:58,948
-He got the video, right?
-For sure.

272
00:20:06,331 --> 00:20:09,125
All right.
Let's go and catch the last one.

273
00:20:09,500 --> 00:20:11,461
-Let's do it!
-All right!

274
00:20:24,557 --> 00:20:26,851
Everyone. Look at the camera.

275
00:20:27,518 --> 00:20:30,188
Check for any more evidence, Seok-jin.

276
00:20:32,273 --> 00:20:34,150
We have the five gentlemen on this side

277
00:20:34,233 --> 00:20:35,443
and especially you.

278
00:20:36,277 --> 00:20:39,489
You all agreed
to accept payment upfront and bonds

279
00:20:39,572 --> 00:20:42,325
in exchange for voting
to withdraw Mr. Yoon's nomination as CEO.

280
00:20:46,829 --> 00:20:49,165
Unfortunately, you won't be
getting those bonds.

281
00:20:49,248 --> 00:20:52,752
The legal team has requested assistance
from the police agency and Interpol.

282
00:20:52,835 --> 00:20:55,046
The assets of that shell company

283
00:20:55,338 --> 00:20:57,382
have been frozen.

284
00:21:01,594 --> 00:21:02,845
What are you waiting for?

285
00:21:03,596 --> 00:21:06,015
Remove those two
for disrupting the meeting!

286
00:21:06,599 --> 00:21:10,019
Excuse me, everyone.
We're the Special Investigation Team.

287
00:21:10,645 --> 00:21:11,854
Ms. Yoon Mi-jin.

288
00:21:15,274 --> 00:21:17,276
Where are you going, ma'am?

289
00:21:19,904 --> 00:21:21,239
Are you trying to run away?

290
00:21:21,322 --> 00:21:22,991
Don't get in my way. Move.

291
00:21:24,117 --> 00:21:26,744
-You little…
-What do you think you're doing?

292
00:21:26,828 --> 00:21:28,955
Let go of me, Yi-jun.

293
00:21:31,332 --> 00:21:32,291
Mi-jin.

294
00:21:35,878 --> 00:21:37,422
It's over.

295
00:21:48,975 --> 00:21:52,562
You're under arrest for embezzlement
under the Specific Economic Crimes Act,

296
00:21:52,645 --> 00:21:55,982
and ordering the murders of Han Eun-young,
Na Man-seok, and Park Min-hwan.

297
00:21:56,399 --> 00:21:57,942
You have the right to an attorney

298
00:21:58,026 --> 00:21:59,610
and the right to remain silent.

299
00:22:00,486 --> 00:22:03,573
Anything you say from this point on
may be used against you in court.

300
00:22:05,742 --> 00:22:07,577
The people you hurt have

301
00:22:07,660 --> 00:22:09,287
finally brought you to justice.

302
00:22:09,996 --> 00:22:11,372
Pay for what you've done.

303
00:22:13,499 --> 00:22:14,417
Murder?

304
00:22:15,543 --> 00:22:17,879
Mi-jin. Hey.

305
00:22:19,088 --> 00:22:21,758
Mi-jin! Have you gone crazy?

306
00:22:22,550 --> 00:22:24,594
Father, wait.

307
00:22:24,677 --> 00:22:26,304
I can explain, okay?

308
00:22:26,387 --> 00:22:28,139
Please get rid of those things first!

309
00:22:28,222 --> 00:22:29,098
Father.

310
00:22:29,807 --> 00:22:31,726
I did it all for Taekang.

311
00:22:31,809 --> 00:22:34,145
I took care of all the nuisance.

312
00:22:35,730 --> 00:22:37,106
-Is that so?
-Father.

313
00:22:37,190 --> 00:22:40,193
I'm the one who should take over
the company after you.

314
00:22:40,276 --> 00:22:42,361
Of your three children,
I'm the most like you.

315
00:22:42,445 --> 00:22:43,905
I should lead the company.

316
00:22:44,572 --> 00:22:46,699
School, marriage, work…

317
00:22:46,783 --> 00:22:48,618
I did everything you told me to!

318
00:22:48,701 --> 00:22:50,161
Actually,

319
00:22:50,870 --> 00:22:52,288
I'll start over.

320
00:22:52,371 --> 00:22:54,373
For Taekang, you listened to me,

321
00:22:54,457 --> 00:22:56,626
took innocent lives, and embezzled money!

322
00:22:56,709 --> 00:22:57,919
For Taekang?

323
00:22:58,419 --> 00:23:00,880
What's next?

324
00:23:01,214 --> 00:23:03,299
Will you sacrifice yourself as well?

325
00:23:06,594 --> 00:23:07,553
Father.

326
00:23:14,560 --> 00:23:15,978
Taekang has consumed you.

327
00:23:20,233 --> 00:23:21,234
You!

328
00:23:24,403 --> 00:23:25,863
You're nothing like me.

329
00:23:30,243 --> 00:23:31,410
Father!

330
00:23:31,869 --> 00:23:33,913
Father!

331
00:23:33,996 --> 00:23:35,248
Father!

332
00:24:01,149 --> 00:24:02,775
All right. Let's go.

333
00:24:02,859 --> 00:24:04,443
Come on.

334
00:24:05,361 --> 00:24:07,446
You need to come with us.

335
00:24:12,326 --> 00:24:14,745
I told you to keep them under control.

336
00:25:17,266 --> 00:25:19,769
She was taken into police custody today.

337
00:25:19,852 --> 00:25:22,021
As well as allegations of
embezzling slush funds,

338
00:25:22,104 --> 00:25:25,066
she is suspected of being involved
in the attack on her brother…

339
00:25:28,361 --> 00:25:30,196
Your stitches have come apart.

340
00:25:30,821 --> 00:25:32,323
I told you not to go out.

341
00:25:32,823 --> 00:25:33,866
Sorry.

342
00:25:34,825 --> 00:25:36,494
I heard you were part of the SMU.

343
00:25:37,119 --> 00:25:38,120
Yes, that's right.

344
00:25:38,204 --> 00:25:39,455
They're amazing.

345
00:25:39,956 --> 00:25:41,457
Which class were you in?

346
00:25:42,792 --> 00:25:44,168
All the nurses on our ward

347
00:25:44,252 --> 00:25:46,337
are going crazy over how cool you are.

348
00:25:48,714 --> 00:25:49,799
Your arm…

349
00:25:56,222 --> 00:25:57,556
It's a letter for you.

350
00:26:00,226 --> 00:26:01,894
Congratulations on being discharged.

351
00:26:06,732 --> 00:26:08,276
Do you know how worried I was?

352
00:26:08,776 --> 00:26:11,737
No!

353
00:26:13,406 --> 00:26:15,533
What? What's the matter?

354
00:26:19,870 --> 00:26:20,871
Look.

355
00:26:21,539 --> 00:26:22,873
I'm going to stay with you.

356
00:26:23,416 --> 00:26:24,500
What?

357
00:26:35,469 --> 00:26:37,096
But I think…

358
00:26:37,805 --> 00:26:38,723
Well…

359
00:26:40,016 --> 00:26:41,892
It's too early for you to be discharged.

360
00:26:41,976 --> 00:26:43,519
Let's get you back to the hospital.

361
00:26:43,602 --> 00:26:46,272
-We settled on outpatient care.
-That's not up for debate!

362
00:26:46,981 --> 00:26:49,567
If you hate the hospital,
why not stay at the chairman's?

363
00:26:49,650 --> 00:26:52,361
Why are you trying to send me off?
I'm still a patient.

364
00:26:52,445 --> 00:26:54,572
Look. I'm happy being with you, but--

365
00:26:54,655 --> 00:26:57,742
Yes, you are.
That's why I should stay with you.

366
00:26:57,825 --> 00:26:59,910
But you're still in pain.
You need a doctor…

367
00:27:00,369 --> 00:27:02,121
-Sorry about that.
-It hurts so much.

368
00:27:02,204 --> 00:27:04,290
-Really?
-I think I need to lie down.

369
00:27:04,623 --> 00:27:05,624
I can't move.

370
00:27:08,169 --> 00:27:09,295
I'm serious.

371
00:27:10,254 --> 00:27:11,213
Fine.

372
00:27:11,672 --> 00:27:13,841
But don't complain
if you're uncomfortable.

373
00:27:13,924 --> 00:27:16,052
Only until your place finishes remodeling.

374
00:27:16,135 --> 00:27:17,595
-Okay.
-It'll be uncomfortable.

375
00:27:17,678 --> 00:27:19,347
My place is tiny.

376
00:27:24,769 --> 00:27:25,728
Did you call me?

377
00:27:25,811 --> 00:27:27,980
-What? Let's go.
-Did you not call me?

378
00:27:28,064 --> 00:27:29,231
-It hurts.
-Careful.

379
00:27:43,537 --> 00:27:44,497
Did you wash up?

380
00:27:44,872 --> 00:27:46,040
Yes, basically.

381
00:27:47,249 --> 00:27:49,377
While you're staying here,
you can use the bed.

382
00:27:49,460 --> 00:27:50,503
I'll sleep on the sofa.

383
00:27:50,586 --> 00:27:52,296
But this is your place.

384
00:27:52,380 --> 00:27:54,048
Who cares whose place it is?

385
00:27:54,131 --> 00:27:55,883
You need to recover.

386
00:27:56,801 --> 00:27:58,886
You were just discharged
from the hospital.

387
00:28:00,513 --> 00:28:01,722
You're a patient too.

388
00:28:02,056 --> 00:28:03,057
I am,

389
00:28:03,140 --> 00:28:04,558
but I'm sturdy.

390
00:28:05,226 --> 00:28:06,602
I'm really fine.

391
00:28:06,685 --> 00:28:09,271
Stop saying you're okay.
See? You're not fine.

392
00:28:10,022 --> 00:28:10,940
Put your legs up.

393
00:28:11,315 --> 00:28:12,441
Goodness.

394
00:28:13,067 --> 00:28:14,151
This is unnecessary.

395
00:28:15,069 --> 00:28:17,863
I just need this pillow.

396
00:28:18,364 --> 00:28:20,574
-Where are you going to sleep?
-On the sofa.

397
00:28:21,826 --> 00:28:24,620
-I'll turn off the lights.
-I'm really okay.

398
00:28:31,293 --> 00:28:32,294
Goodnight.

399
00:28:33,087 --> 00:28:34,046
Goodnight.

400
00:28:59,989 --> 00:29:01,824
-I…
-You said you'd do that thing for me.

401
00:29:02,533 --> 00:29:03,617
What?

402
00:29:04,660 --> 00:29:06,287
-Tell me.
-You tell me first.

403
00:29:06,996 --> 00:29:08,122
We should sleep together.

404
00:29:08,205 --> 00:29:10,374
-What?
-See?

405
00:29:10,458 --> 00:29:12,334
You could suddenly be in pain like now.

406
00:29:12,418 --> 00:29:14,003
I can't take care of you from there.

407
00:29:14,086 --> 00:29:15,671
Are you okay?

408
00:29:15,754 --> 00:29:16,755
I'm a patient too.

409
00:29:16,839 --> 00:29:19,216
Come to think of it,
who's going to look after me?

410
00:29:19,300 --> 00:29:21,260
-That's me.
-That's right.

411
00:29:21,969 --> 00:29:22,928
This makes sense.

412
00:29:24,763 --> 00:29:25,723
You're right.

413
00:29:26,640 --> 00:29:29,059
But what did you say earlier?

414
00:29:31,270 --> 00:29:33,481
The last line of defense. Remember?

415
00:29:34,231 --> 00:29:36,150
I'm a woman of my word.

416
00:29:36,734 --> 00:29:37,943
At times,

417
00:29:39,612 --> 00:29:40,863
it feels like

418
00:29:41,739 --> 00:29:43,407
you came to me to save me.

419
00:29:43,491 --> 00:29:46,494
At times?
I'm the one who's always saving you.

420
00:29:47,411 --> 00:29:49,788
And I'll keep saving you.

421
00:29:50,706 --> 00:29:51,540
Thanks.

422
00:30:19,860 --> 00:30:21,695
-It's my parents.
-They know the passcode?

423
00:30:23,030 --> 00:30:24,365
I'm so sorry!

424
00:30:26,283 --> 00:30:27,701
Mom! Dad!

425
00:30:30,746 --> 00:30:31,956
Do it properly!

426
00:30:32,831 --> 00:30:35,960
He's also injured.

427
00:30:36,043 --> 00:30:38,212
And making us kneel down is going too far.

428
00:30:38,295 --> 00:30:40,297
They never told us to kneel.
We just did it.

429
00:30:40,381 --> 00:30:42,925
So, tell us.

430
00:30:43,008 --> 00:30:44,969
We only kissed, ma'am.

431
00:30:45,052 --> 00:30:46,387
You little…

432
00:30:50,057 --> 00:30:51,559
Not that.

433
00:30:54,103 --> 00:30:55,604
Are you really from a rich family?

434
00:30:57,064 --> 00:31:00,025
Would coming from wealth help right now?

435
00:31:00,192 --> 00:31:02,361
Like winning your favor, for instance?

436
00:31:02,444 --> 00:31:03,737
And if it doesn't?

437
00:31:04,488 --> 00:31:05,656
Then it's a relief.

438
00:31:05,739 --> 00:31:07,741
I think I'm about to get disowned.

439
00:31:08,576 --> 00:31:11,161
-That's a shame. It's Taekang.
-What's wrong with you?

440
00:31:14,873 --> 00:31:16,375
We're an ordinary family.

441
00:31:16,875 --> 00:31:18,544
Jae-hee had an ordinary childhood.

442
00:31:19,920 --> 00:31:21,589
I'm sorry to be blunt,

443
00:31:22,047 --> 00:31:23,757
but Jae-hee isn't ordinary at all.

444
00:31:24,258 --> 00:31:26,427
In my eyes, she is beautiful,

445
00:31:27,386 --> 00:31:29,430
cool, and cute.

446
00:31:30,055 --> 00:31:32,683
More importantly, she's precious.

447
00:31:37,438 --> 00:31:38,731
Hands up properly!

448
00:31:41,692 --> 00:31:43,569
What if your powerful family

449
00:31:43,652 --> 00:31:45,112
doesn't approve of Jae-hee?

450
00:31:45,321 --> 00:31:46,196
Well,

451
00:31:47,114 --> 00:31:48,282
that's why

452
00:31:48,616 --> 00:31:51,243
I can't ask you
to let Jae-hee come live with me just yet.

453
00:31:51,619 --> 00:31:55,205
Instead, when everything is all set,
I will come visit you.

454
00:31:55,289 --> 00:31:58,167
And she already agreed
to take responsibility for me as well.

455
00:31:58,959 --> 00:32:00,794
-Who's taking responsibility for who?
-Who?

456
00:32:01,420 --> 00:32:03,922
I am taking responsibility for him.

457
00:32:07,384 --> 00:32:10,387
I'm grateful that you saved her life.

458
00:32:10,471 --> 00:32:13,766
But if she hadn't gone undercover,
none of this would've happened.

459
00:32:14,350 --> 00:32:15,809
And your wealth is a bit much.

460
00:32:16,268 --> 00:32:17,561
I'm not sure about you.

461
00:32:18,812 --> 00:32:20,439
Honey, get up. Let's leave.

462
00:32:21,148 --> 00:32:22,566
Keep your hands up.

463
00:32:31,033 --> 00:32:32,159
Don't sleep together.

464
00:32:32,242 --> 00:32:34,411
You have a bed and a sofa.

465
00:32:36,246 --> 00:32:37,164
Yes, ma'am.

466
00:32:39,458 --> 00:32:42,878
She gets more cranky around mealtime.
Please understand.

467
00:32:45,214 --> 00:32:47,925
LEGAL TEAM KIM SI-HYUN

468
00:33:03,732 --> 00:33:04,817
I didn't order it.

469
00:33:05,192 --> 00:33:09,238
Your boyfriend told me to look after you
because drinking upsets your stomach.

470
00:33:12,157 --> 00:33:14,993
Why does he act all worried
when he's not even my boyfriend?

471
00:33:15,077 --> 00:33:19,373
If he's not your boyfriend,
why is he so worried about you?

472
00:33:20,874 --> 00:33:21,959
What did he say?

473
00:33:22,042 --> 00:33:26,338
He told me to limit you
to one bottle of soju when you drink.

474
00:33:27,965 --> 00:33:30,175
Why is he meddling
when he's not my boyfriend?

475
00:33:30,259 --> 00:33:33,637
That not-boyfriend of yours
paid hundreds of thousands of won upfront.

476
00:33:34,930 --> 00:33:38,434
You can chug down soju straight
without even turning red,

477
00:33:38,892 --> 00:33:41,145
but I guess love
must be stronger than soju.

478
00:33:44,732 --> 00:33:45,858
That's not it.

479
00:33:50,904 --> 00:33:51,864
Ma'am.

480
00:33:52,281 --> 00:33:53,449
Can I get a bowl to-go?

481
00:33:54,658 --> 00:33:56,410
SAESUPGIL HAEJANGGUK

482
00:33:57,369 --> 00:34:00,205
Why do you keep texting me
that you haven't eaten?

483
00:34:00,289 --> 00:34:02,499
You must've been worried
about me going hungry.

484
00:34:02,583 --> 00:34:05,294
I do the same for Secretary Woo.
I buy her gimbap, too.

485
00:34:05,377 --> 00:34:08,130
But this is
from your favorite gamjatang place.

486
00:34:08,672 --> 00:34:10,132
Anyway, here's what I did today--

487
00:34:10,215 --> 00:34:11,175
Enough.

488
00:34:12,843 --> 00:34:14,094
Stop texting me.

489
00:34:15,387 --> 00:34:18,599
What time you woke up,
went to work, had coffee…

490
00:34:18,932 --> 00:34:21,935
Why do I have to keep track
of every little thing like some stalker?

491
00:34:24,855 --> 00:34:27,941
I'm not new to relationships.
I can't promise you everlasting love.

492
00:34:29,151 --> 00:34:30,068
But…

493
00:34:31,820 --> 00:34:33,405
I will act responsibly.

494
00:34:36,950 --> 00:34:38,494
Heart, star, or flowers?

495
00:34:38,577 --> 00:34:40,120
Choose one.

496
00:34:40,537 --> 00:34:42,456
I'll carve it over that indelible scar,

497
00:34:42,915 --> 00:34:43,999
every day.

498
00:34:46,877 --> 00:34:48,045
What a smooth talker.

499
00:34:48,128 --> 00:34:49,922
What can you even do when you're so busy?

500
00:34:50,005 --> 00:34:52,508
That's right. It breaks my heart

501
00:34:52,591 --> 00:34:54,885
that little brat made me
clean up after him

502
00:34:55,427 --> 00:34:56,887
while he gets to have fun!

503
00:34:56,970 --> 00:34:58,847
I want to go on dates!

504
00:34:58,931 --> 00:35:01,517
I want to go to this restaurant!
It was really good.

505
00:35:03,352 --> 00:35:04,686
Did you just buy mine?

506
00:35:04,770 --> 00:35:06,355
Go ahead and eat.

507
00:35:06,980 --> 00:35:08,148
Thank you.

508
00:35:18,325 --> 00:35:20,577
I'll figure it out soon, so just wait.

509
00:35:20,661 --> 00:35:22,871
I'm not your errand boy.

510
00:35:23,121 --> 00:35:25,791
There are two other ways
to piss off a good lawyer.

511
00:35:25,874 --> 00:35:27,584
One. Asking them to buy matching rings.

512
00:35:27,668 --> 00:35:29,253
Two. Rubbing it in with the rings.

513
00:35:29,336 --> 00:35:31,505
Good job. I'll tell you the size soon.

514
00:35:31,588 --> 00:35:33,715
I'm just going to buy
the most expensive one.

515
00:35:34,132 --> 00:35:36,134
You'd better not
complain about the design.

516
00:35:36,218 --> 00:35:37,886
Okay. Thanks.

517
00:35:40,430 --> 00:35:42,850
I didn't know he knew how to thank people.

518
00:35:42,933 --> 00:35:44,601
Matching rings, confession,

519
00:35:44,685 --> 00:35:46,854
and redefining our relationship. Perfect.

520
00:35:48,647 --> 00:35:50,482
-Did you choose?
-No.

521
00:35:50,983 --> 00:35:53,819
Take your time. Pick your favorite one.

522
00:35:53,902 --> 00:35:55,070
Okay,

523
00:35:55,529 --> 00:35:56,655
then…

524
00:35:57,990 --> 00:36:00,492
-How about this one?
-That one's cute.

525
00:36:00,701 --> 00:36:01,952
Do you like cute things?

526
00:36:02,035 --> 00:36:03,996
Not really. It just looks tasty.

527
00:36:06,540 --> 00:36:08,250
But this one is also…

528
00:36:08,333 --> 00:36:10,752
This is fancy. Is this what you like?

529
00:36:10,836 --> 00:36:12,421
It's just that it looks tasty too.

530
00:36:16,508 --> 00:36:19,803
You know what? This is the best.

531
00:36:19,887 --> 00:36:22,389
This one is simple.
You like to keep it classic?

532
00:36:22,472 --> 00:36:23,724
It looks the tastiest.

533
00:36:25,517 --> 00:36:27,895
Excuse me. Can we have this one?

534
00:36:27,978 --> 00:36:28,812
Okay.

535
00:36:30,272 --> 00:36:31,315
By the way,

536
00:36:33,734 --> 00:36:36,320
you can't seem
to leave my hand alone today.

537
00:36:36,987 --> 00:36:37,821
Right?

538
00:36:42,618 --> 00:36:43,785
Want me to read your palm?

539
00:36:43,869 --> 00:36:46,246
-What?
-I'm an expert at this.

540
00:36:46,955 --> 00:36:47,789
Let's see.

541
00:36:49,708 --> 00:36:50,584
It's good.

542
00:36:51,460 --> 00:36:54,504
You can just hold my hand if you want to.

543
00:37:01,178 --> 00:37:02,095
DAD

544
00:37:02,179 --> 00:37:03,597
It's my dad.

545
00:37:04,932 --> 00:37:05,766
Hey, Dad.

546
00:37:06,725 --> 00:37:07,768
What?

547
00:37:07,851 --> 00:37:09,770
It's just for an hour, okay?

548
00:37:10,145 --> 00:37:12,064
I can't cover for you longer than that.

549
00:37:12,147 --> 00:37:14,691
I was supposed to have dinner out
with Yi-jun.

550
00:37:14,775 --> 00:37:16,652
Push the reservation back an hour.

551
00:37:16,735 --> 00:37:18,695
Fine. Okay.

552
00:37:21,156 --> 00:37:22,699
Even dog crap has its uses.

553
00:37:22,783 --> 00:37:26,036
But this man is
good for absolutely nothing.

554
00:37:26,119 --> 00:37:28,038
-Thanks.
-Here you go.

555
00:37:28,205 --> 00:37:30,248
-Did you watch the news?
-What news?

556
00:37:30,332 --> 00:37:32,459
Taekang is in chaos right now.

557
00:37:32,793 --> 00:37:35,504
Right. The eldest daughter
embezzled money or something, right?

558
00:37:35,587 --> 00:37:37,839
She almost murdered
her little brother, right?

559
00:37:38,382 --> 00:37:40,759
You know how my son works at Taekang?

560
00:37:41,051 --> 00:37:43,804
It's just the rich fighting over money.

561
00:37:43,971 --> 00:37:45,472
-Jeez.
-Fighting over money?

562
00:37:45,555 --> 00:37:49,101
They say the youngest brother
ran wild for years.

563
00:37:49,184 --> 00:37:51,103
He was a reckless troublemaker.

564
00:37:51,186 --> 00:37:54,314
-He was just lucky to be born into the…
-I'll have a word with her.

565
00:37:55,857 --> 00:37:56,817
It's fine.

566
00:37:57,484 --> 00:37:58,819
It's your mother's store.

567
00:38:00,070 --> 00:38:00,946
I'll wait nearby.

568
00:38:01,029 --> 00:38:02,489
He's not a troublemaker.

569
00:38:02,572 --> 00:38:04,241
Lucky to be born into that family?

570
00:38:04,491 --> 00:38:06,618
It's a wonder

571
00:38:06,702 --> 00:38:09,371
he didn't turn out spoiled and reckless.

572
00:38:09,454 --> 00:38:10,789
You don't even know anything.

573
00:38:10,872 --> 00:38:13,542
Why are you getting all riled up?

574
00:38:13,625 --> 00:38:15,002
Anyone would think

575
00:38:15,085 --> 00:38:16,920
I was badmouthing your son.

576
00:38:17,004 --> 00:38:19,339
Who knows?
He might become part of my family!

577
00:38:19,423 --> 00:38:21,508
You have no idea how dignified he looks!

578
00:38:21,591 --> 00:38:22,718
-I think
-Now get out.

579
00:38:22,801 --> 00:38:24,803
Mom likes you.

580
00:38:25,178 --> 00:38:26,763
She only seems harsh on the outside.

581
00:38:30,267 --> 00:38:32,477
Suk-ja, we're leaving now!

582
00:38:32,811 --> 00:38:34,104
-Let's go.
-Let's go.

583
00:38:34,187 --> 00:38:35,731
-Come on.
-Let's go.

584
00:38:36,231 --> 00:38:37,524
Is Ms. Cho Suk-ja here?

585
00:38:37,607 --> 00:38:38,859
That's me.

586
00:38:39,693 --> 00:38:42,821
Taekang Group's Managing Director Yoon
chose these gifts himself.

587
00:38:43,947 --> 00:38:45,032
-What?
-Taekang Group?

588
00:38:45,115 --> 00:38:46,408
-Taekang?
-Managing director?

589
00:38:46,491 --> 00:38:48,368
-What's all this?
-Why would he?

590
00:39:02,132 --> 00:39:04,426
Your future son-in-law is here
to say hello.

591
00:39:05,635 --> 00:39:06,511
Future son-in-law?

592
00:39:09,514 --> 00:39:11,558
-Mother, these flowers are for you.
-Mother?

593
00:39:11,641 --> 00:39:13,602
In-laws with a billionaire family?

594
00:39:13,685 --> 00:39:15,937
-My goodness.
-Unbelievable.

595
00:39:17,522 --> 00:39:19,983
I couldn't bring much on short notice.

596
00:39:21,693 --> 00:39:22,861
Thanks.

597
00:39:26,490 --> 00:39:29,117
Gosh, you look very happy, Ms. Cho.

598
00:39:31,495 --> 00:39:35,248
So he managed to win her mother's heart
instead of redefining their relationship.

599
00:39:35,332 --> 00:39:37,209
Well, that's an awkward sort of success.

600
00:39:37,292 --> 00:39:40,212
But the two are technically dating, right?

601
00:39:40,295 --> 00:39:41,671
Ms. Kang is way too popular.

602
00:39:41,755 --> 00:39:43,924
He wants to make it clear
that she is his woman.

603
00:39:44,007 --> 00:39:45,592
Why all that drama about breaking up

604
00:39:45,675 --> 00:39:47,886
in the first place
if he's going to be like this?

605
00:39:48,762 --> 00:39:49,846
He was being dramatic.

606
00:39:50,138 --> 00:39:52,933
He went back again this morning,
determined to succeed this time.

607
00:39:53,016 --> 00:39:53,892
Succeed at what?

608
00:39:56,269 --> 00:39:57,479
You made it?

609
00:39:58,355 --> 00:40:00,190
Will you be okay meeting him?

610
00:40:01,650 --> 00:40:03,360
I'm here to question a witness.

611
00:40:03,443 --> 00:40:05,529
I'd be here
even for the chairman's grandfather.

612
00:40:06,947 --> 00:40:07,781
Good luck.

613
00:40:07,864 --> 00:40:09,157
Shall we go, ma'am?

614
00:40:09,908 --> 00:40:10,784
Yes, sir.

615
00:40:11,284 --> 00:40:13,036
KUNMANDU

616
00:40:15,539 --> 00:40:19,000
I don't know if we should be
making a billionaire do this kind of work.

617
00:40:23,588 --> 00:40:24,714
Ma'am.

618
00:40:24,798 --> 00:40:27,801
Could you teach me how to make gimbap?

619
00:40:28,385 --> 00:40:29,970
-Gimbap?
-Yes.

620
00:40:30,053 --> 00:40:32,222
I have a reason to make it.

621
00:40:40,313 --> 00:40:42,190
47. PICK HIM UP IN THE RAIN
WITH AN UMBRELLA

622
00:40:42,274 --> 00:40:43,900
48: MAKE GIMBAP AND GO ON A PICNIC

623
00:40:47,237 --> 00:40:49,156
Make gimbap and go on a picnic.

624
00:40:51,116 --> 00:40:53,243
All the things
I want to do with Yoon Yi-jun.

625
00:40:54,536 --> 00:40:57,205
What kind of gimbap does Jae-hee like?

626
00:40:57,581 --> 00:40:59,332
She likes bibimbap,

627
00:40:59,416 --> 00:41:01,084
so she might like vegetable gimbap.

628
00:41:01,168 --> 00:41:03,295
She likes spicy food as well,

629
00:41:03,378 --> 00:41:04,796
so maybe chili pepper gimbap?

630
00:41:05,505 --> 00:41:07,465
What kind of gimbap do you like, ma'am?

631
00:41:07,549 --> 00:41:09,259
She likes grilled intestines.

632
00:41:10,677 --> 00:41:12,262
Can you make gimbap with it?

633
00:41:16,725 --> 00:41:17,559
Mom.

634
00:41:18,018 --> 00:41:20,520
Is it hard to make gimbap?

635
00:41:20,854 --> 00:41:21,688
Why do you ask?

636
00:41:23,732 --> 00:41:26,943
It's not hard, but it takes time.
Why do you ask?

637
00:41:27,652 --> 00:41:28,737
Well

638
00:41:29,321 --> 00:41:30,947
Even with a top chef

639
00:41:31,031 --> 00:41:33,700
packing a lavish spread for every picnic,

640
00:41:34,576 --> 00:41:36,494
he envied other kids' homemade gimbap.

641
00:41:38,205 --> 00:41:39,789
Well, I have a friend.

642
00:41:39,873 --> 00:41:42,459
And you know how we go on picnics
when we're children?

643
00:41:42,959 --> 00:41:45,503
They wanted to try homemade gimbap
ever since then.

644
00:41:46,671 --> 00:41:47,547
Who is this friend?

645
00:41:49,090 --> 00:41:51,009
-Don't worry about it.
-Is it a guy?

646
00:41:51,092 --> 00:41:52,510
They're not a woman.

647
00:41:52,594 --> 00:41:53,511
Seok-jin?

648
00:41:54,137 --> 00:41:56,348
Why would you bring him up?

649
00:41:56,556 --> 00:41:58,850
Anyway, there's someone.

650
00:41:59,601 --> 00:42:01,144
He's a bit of a jerk,

651
00:42:01,895 --> 00:42:04,606
but he was super nice
to the old lady at the amusement park.

652
00:42:04,898 --> 00:42:06,358
So he seems like a decent guy.

653
00:42:11,571 --> 00:42:13,365
-So that's when.
-What?

654
00:42:15,617 --> 00:42:17,285
Eggs, spinach,

655
00:42:17,369 --> 00:42:19,162
and cucumbers are in the fridge.

656
00:42:19,246 --> 00:42:20,205
Yes, ma'am.

657
00:42:24,417 --> 00:42:25,627
Oh boy.

658
00:42:28,088 --> 00:42:31,091
I'd like to ask one last question, sir.

659
00:42:32,175 --> 00:42:33,635
This case began

660
00:42:34,219 --> 00:42:36,388
with a power struggle over succession.

661
00:42:36,471 --> 00:42:39,599
In the process, Yoon Mi-jin
embezzled funds for her slush fund

662
00:42:40,183 --> 00:42:41,643
and plotted to take over Taekang,

663
00:42:41,726 --> 00:42:44,062
preparing for board meetings
and shareholder meetings.

664
00:42:44,145 --> 00:42:46,273
You've also taken a hit.

665
00:42:46,898 --> 00:42:49,609
We believe that you provided a motive
for her crimes

666
00:42:49,693 --> 00:42:51,695
by pitting your children
against each other.

667
00:42:52,320 --> 00:42:53,363
Do you agree?

668
00:42:56,491 --> 00:42:58,201
I did pit them against each other.

669
00:42:58,285 --> 00:43:00,370
I gave them weapons.

670
00:43:00,453 --> 00:43:04,291
But how they used those weapons
was their own choice.

671
00:43:04,374 --> 00:43:05,917
Same goes for Yi-jun.

672
00:43:06,584 --> 00:43:08,169
You want to hold me responsible.

673
00:43:08,253 --> 00:43:12,132
But this was simply the process
of an unqualified one being weeded out.

674
00:43:14,467 --> 00:43:15,385
Yes, sir.

675
00:43:16,928 --> 00:43:20,265
The chairman
was exercising his business judgment,

676
00:43:20,765 --> 00:43:24,060
while Yoon Mi-jin's misconduct
was an individual criminal act.

677
00:43:25,854 --> 00:43:29,524
If you keep asking speculative questions,
we'll exercise the right to a defense.

678
00:43:31,276 --> 00:43:32,235
Let's wrap this up.

679
00:43:44,664 --> 00:43:46,374
According to your ways,

680
00:43:51,046 --> 00:43:52,714
you owe me a debt.

681
00:43:56,426 --> 00:43:57,302
So?

682
00:43:58,011 --> 00:43:59,054
You want to be repaid?

683
00:44:00,430 --> 00:44:02,182
Everyone envies Yoon Yi-jun.

684
00:44:02,849 --> 00:44:04,309
But I pity him.

685
00:44:06,186 --> 00:44:07,437
"Pity"?

686
00:44:09,230 --> 00:44:10,065
How dare you?

687
00:44:10,148 --> 00:44:13,234
Your son was injured and lying in bed.

688
00:44:13,735 --> 00:44:15,362
Is it so hard to ask if he's okay?

689
00:44:16,279 --> 00:44:18,490
I won't take a loss when it comes to you.

690
00:44:18,990 --> 00:44:20,992
I'll settle the debt you owe me myself.

691
00:44:28,166 --> 00:44:30,877
And from now on, I won't leave him alone.

692
00:44:31,669 --> 00:44:33,213
I almost died.

693
00:44:33,546 --> 00:44:35,131
I'm not afraid of you.

694
00:44:43,932 --> 00:44:45,475
Gosh, I'm sorry.

695
00:44:45,767 --> 00:44:47,143
I don't think I can go quickly.

696
00:44:47,227 --> 00:44:49,687
No, Jae-hee.
You need to come as soon as possible.

697
00:44:49,771 --> 00:44:52,107
I have to file a report
on the witness interview.

698
00:44:52,190 --> 00:44:55,443
Hey, I asked you for the report ages ago!

699
00:44:55,902 --> 00:44:59,030
Jeez, she will never learn
to listen to me.

700
00:44:59,114 --> 00:45:02,325
-I hate this damn team…
-I don't think Captain will let me go.

701
00:45:03,034 --> 00:45:05,328
Really? Then give me ten minutes.

702
00:45:05,412 --> 00:45:07,372
Why aren't you rolling gimbap, son?

703
00:45:07,455 --> 00:45:08,623
I'll be right there.

704
00:45:09,374 --> 00:45:10,959
Jae-hee, come quickly.

705
00:45:11,042 --> 00:45:12,293
I need to hang up now.

706
00:45:16,714 --> 00:45:18,049
Can you massage my shoulders?

707
00:45:19,342 --> 00:45:22,053
You didn't even roll many.
We're just getting started.

708
00:45:22,554 --> 00:45:23,471
Ten minutes?

709
00:45:25,056 --> 00:45:25,890
What?

710
00:45:29,185 --> 00:45:32,355
TAEKANG MANAGING DIRECTOR YOON YI-JUN
SHARES THANKS TO INVESTIGATION TEAM

711
00:45:32,439 --> 00:45:34,732
I didn't really do much.

712
00:45:34,816 --> 00:45:37,777
I mean,
investigating is my job, after all.

713
00:45:38,319 --> 00:45:39,821
What do you mean, lucky?

714
00:45:39,904 --> 00:45:43,032
Luck always comes to those who work hard.

715
00:45:44,826 --> 00:45:45,743
Hold on.

716
00:45:45,827 --> 00:45:48,663
I'm getting so many calls
after the news broke.

717
00:45:48,746 --> 00:45:50,748
Congratulations on your promotion, sir!

718
00:45:50,832 --> 00:45:53,334
-Come on.
-Everyone, a round of applause!

719
00:45:59,716 --> 00:46:00,800
Did you hear that?

720
00:46:01,801 --> 00:46:05,305
I'm not a captain anymore!
I got promoted, man!

721
00:46:08,808 --> 00:46:09,934
Hold on.

722
00:46:10,018 --> 00:46:11,686
Hey, about the report…

723
00:46:12,729 --> 00:46:14,063
You write it!

724
00:46:14,522 --> 00:46:16,733
All right. You can go.

725
00:46:16,816 --> 00:46:17,692
Yes?

726
00:46:24,699 --> 00:46:25,867
This is making me nervous.

727
00:46:25,950 --> 00:46:28,495
My mom rolls at least 100 rolls of gimbap.

728
00:46:30,205 --> 00:46:33,208
She made 200 rolls today.

729
00:46:33,583 --> 00:46:34,667
-What, 200 rolls?
-Yes.

730
00:46:35,251 --> 00:46:36,252
Good job.

731
00:46:37,045 --> 00:46:38,421
-Is it good?
-Yes.

732
00:46:39,130 --> 00:46:40,089
You know,

733
00:46:41,382 --> 00:46:42,634
I really like your mother.

734
00:46:43,426 --> 00:46:44,969
She treats me like a son now.

735
00:46:45,845 --> 00:46:47,514
-You must be happy.
-Yes.

736
00:46:49,224 --> 00:46:53,394
We talked a lot while making gimbap.

737
00:46:53,478 --> 00:46:55,688
I think she's a kind person.

738
00:46:56,731 --> 00:47:01,319
And you grew up to be a good person
like your parents.

739
00:47:07,075 --> 00:47:08,368
Did you visit her?

740
00:47:13,665 --> 00:47:14,666
Yes.

741
00:47:16,793 --> 00:47:18,294
VISITATION ROOM

742
00:47:31,140 --> 00:47:34,602
Apologize to the people you've hurt.
Show some remorse.

743
00:47:36,479 --> 00:47:37,605
No.

744
00:47:38,982 --> 00:47:41,776
You should be the one apologizing, not me.

745
00:47:44,153 --> 00:47:45,196
Yi-jun.

746
00:47:46,447 --> 00:47:48,616
They all died because of you.

747
00:47:53,371 --> 00:47:54,414
Why…

748
00:47:57,458 --> 00:47:59,294
Why did you start looking for the money?

749
00:48:00,128 --> 00:48:01,879
Why did you covet my position?

750
00:48:05,508 --> 00:48:07,927
I exposed everything at the board meeting,

751
00:48:08,011 --> 00:48:09,762
so you won't get out of here easily.

752
00:48:13,641 --> 00:48:15,143
I've chosen a law firm.

753
00:48:15,226 --> 00:48:16,853
I'll be out of here soon.

754
00:48:17,312 --> 00:48:18,813
Didn't you hear from Father?

755
00:48:19,272 --> 00:48:21,858
A parent should scold their child
if they cause trouble.

756
00:48:22,734 --> 00:48:25,528
He said you wouldn't be granted
a suspension of your sentence.

757
00:48:25,612 --> 00:48:27,405
You're stuck here.

758
00:48:27,488 --> 00:48:28,489
Yi-jun!

759
00:48:28,573 --> 00:48:29,866
Thanks to you,

760
00:48:30,700 --> 00:48:32,243
I've become stronger.

761
00:48:33,161 --> 00:48:36,539
I won't fall apart
and I'll live responsibly

762
00:48:38,374 --> 00:48:39,917
for the people I care about.

763
00:48:42,503 --> 00:48:45,256
Thank you, Mi-jin.

764
00:49:02,315 --> 00:49:04,484
Thanks to you,

765
00:49:05,318 --> 00:49:07,070
I've grown stronger, Jae-hee.

766
00:49:08,738 --> 00:49:09,739
Thank you.

767
00:49:12,283 --> 00:49:13,242
Same.

768
00:49:14,619 --> 00:49:15,495
Thank you.

769
00:49:15,578 --> 00:49:17,455
Let's stop thanking each other.

770
00:49:18,539 --> 00:49:19,582
Close your eyes.

771
00:49:21,000 --> 00:49:22,085
Okay.

772
00:49:28,716 --> 00:49:30,718
Kang Jae-hee. I, Yoon Yi-jun,

773
00:49:31,719 --> 00:49:32,887
love…

774
00:49:33,763 --> 00:49:35,473
-What?
-I love you.

775
00:49:36,724 --> 00:49:38,935
Wait. I also prepared…

776
00:49:39,852 --> 00:49:40,687
When…

777
00:49:40,770 --> 00:49:42,021
No, Jae-hee.

778
00:49:42,355 --> 00:49:44,816
I can't let you have this.
I have to be the one to do it.

779
00:49:44,899 --> 00:49:48,236
Calm down.
Now we have two matching pairs of rings.

780
00:49:48,695 --> 00:49:49,779
We can wear both.

781
00:49:51,072 --> 00:49:52,031
That's a good idea.

782
00:50:11,426 --> 00:50:13,761
-I love you.
-I love you too.

783
00:50:15,471 --> 00:50:18,683
Let's cherish each other
for the rest of our lives,

784
00:50:19,225 --> 00:50:20,935
in equal measure.

785
00:50:21,018 --> 00:50:22,937
In equal measure.

786
00:50:23,020 --> 00:50:24,105
Okay.

787
00:50:26,983 --> 00:50:28,609
-My heart races
-This is pretty.

788
00:50:28,943 --> 00:50:30,695
-so much
-Look.

789
00:50:31,863 --> 00:50:33,573
that it actually hurts.

790
00:50:35,074 --> 00:50:38,453
You're guilty of stealing my heart.

791
00:50:38,953 --> 00:50:41,289
In that case,
you should be serving a life sentence.

792
00:50:41,372 --> 00:50:44,333
This won't do.
We should just handcuff each other.

793
00:50:45,042 --> 00:50:46,043
Give me the key.

794
00:50:46,127 --> 00:50:48,296
I'll throw it far away.

795
00:50:48,755 --> 00:50:49,839
MA HUI-DO

796
00:50:53,885 --> 00:50:54,886
Goodbye, sir.

797
00:50:55,762 --> 00:50:56,804
Good grief.

798
00:51:12,528 --> 00:51:15,323
-Here you go. Enjoy.
-Thank you.

799
00:51:15,740 --> 00:51:17,325
-Thank you.
-Look at this.

800
00:51:17,408 --> 00:51:19,076
Enjoy your meal.

801
00:51:19,160 --> 00:51:20,536
There's more inside.

802
00:51:22,830 --> 00:51:24,499
I never imagined

803
00:51:24,582 --> 00:51:27,043
I'd eat gimbap made by a billionaire.

804
00:51:27,126 --> 00:51:27,960
Hello.

805
00:51:28,044 --> 00:51:30,421
-Thanks, Jae-hee.
-This one doesn't have cucumbers.

806
00:51:30,505 --> 00:51:32,131
-Thanks.
-Thanks!

807
00:51:32,215 --> 00:51:33,716
It's really good.

808
00:51:33,800 --> 00:51:36,302
The new recruit we're getting
came on a motorcycle.

809
00:51:36,385 --> 00:51:38,304
She asked me where to park and stuff.

810
00:51:38,387 --> 00:51:40,598
-A new recruit?
-Did I not tell you?

811
00:51:44,101 --> 00:51:45,394
She's here. This way!

812
00:52:01,452 --> 00:52:02,495
BAEK GO-JIN

813
00:52:02,578 --> 00:52:05,331
Hello! I've been assigned
to the Special Investigations Team.

814
00:52:05,414 --> 00:52:06,707
My name is Baek Go-jin.

815
00:52:08,251 --> 00:52:09,961
I joined to be like Detective Kang.

816
00:52:11,045 --> 00:52:13,881
-I'll work hard to take down the bad guys!
-I love it!

817
00:52:19,512 --> 00:52:20,513
What's your name again?

818
00:52:20,596 --> 00:52:21,806
Detective Baek?

819
00:52:22,390 --> 00:52:23,307
Do you like gimbap?

820
00:52:25,226 --> 00:52:26,394
This can't be real.

821
00:52:26,769 --> 00:52:28,354
She's a fan of mine.

822
00:52:28,771 --> 00:52:30,022
I am.

823
00:52:43,995 --> 00:52:45,079
This is my place.

824
00:52:45,413 --> 00:52:46,664
Why are you here?

825
00:52:47,039 --> 00:52:50,167
Wouldn't it be weird if another woman
appeared in front of you?

826
00:52:51,043 --> 00:52:53,129
We're neighbors, for now.

827
00:52:55,339 --> 00:52:58,009
I brought this to share since I moved in.

828
00:53:01,387 --> 00:53:04,891
It's a peach-plum flavor,
so it's sweet and tangy.

829
00:53:04,974 --> 00:53:06,601
It's easy to eat as well.

830
00:53:06,684 --> 00:53:08,644
-Also--
-You're sharing since you moved in?

831
00:53:08,728 --> 00:53:10,813
"Heart, star, and flowers."

832
00:53:11,480 --> 00:53:12,773
Did you not mean those words?

833
00:53:12,857 --> 00:53:14,525
I totally meant them.

834
00:53:14,609 --> 00:53:16,319
That's why I made a choice.

835
00:53:16,402 --> 00:53:18,446
I chose to be your neighbor for now.

836
00:53:19,280 --> 00:53:21,365
Do you have an electric drill at home?

837
00:53:21,449 --> 00:53:22,783
Of course.

838
00:53:22,867 --> 00:53:24,493
Let me borrow it tomorrow afternoon.

839
00:53:24,577 --> 00:53:25,953
When is the housewarming party?

840
00:53:26,162 --> 00:53:27,371
I'm ready.

841
00:53:29,373 --> 00:53:30,708
You also got some?

842
00:53:31,208 --> 00:53:33,711
There's nothing like gimbap
for a housewarming party.

843
00:53:33,794 --> 00:53:35,588
With instant noodles and beer?

844
00:53:35,671 --> 00:53:37,173
You really get me, don't you?

845
00:53:38,883 --> 00:53:41,886
Let's give our relationship a shot.

846
00:53:44,972 --> 00:53:46,933
-I'd love that.
-I love it too.

847
00:53:49,685 --> 00:53:51,270
You sure made a big fuss of it.

848
00:53:54,065 --> 00:53:56,776
You have to cut away the rot
for new growth to emerge.

849
00:53:57,443 --> 00:54:00,279
You found one thing
and now you're acting all high and mighty.

850
00:54:00,821 --> 00:54:01,906
You know what?

851
00:54:02,698 --> 00:54:05,409
You're always picking fights with me.

852
00:54:06,410 --> 00:54:08,955
I can't help but think
that you're obsessed with me.

853
00:54:13,709 --> 00:54:17,672
I never thought I'd see the day
I'd find you more human than anyone.

854
00:54:18,297 --> 00:54:19,298
Whatever.

855
00:54:25,221 --> 00:54:26,055
Father.

856
00:54:27,181 --> 00:54:28,349
Goodbye, then.

857
00:54:36,941 --> 00:54:38,651
-Father.
-Yes.

858
00:54:40,653 --> 00:54:42,655
Can I ask you a question?

859
00:54:44,782 --> 00:54:46,033
Do you like gimbap?

860
00:54:52,081 --> 00:54:53,332
I knew it.

861
00:55:00,214 --> 00:55:01,632
What's wrong with him?

862
00:55:02,008 --> 00:55:03,676
-Na-jung.
-Yes?

863
00:55:04,301 --> 00:55:05,428
Do you like gimbap?

864
00:55:07,930 --> 00:55:08,889
What's with you now?

865
00:55:10,349 --> 00:55:11,434
I'm not sure.

866
00:55:13,227 --> 00:55:16,439
My goodness.
This is what you call a proper house.

867
00:55:16,814 --> 00:55:19,400
This is practically a stadium.

868
00:55:19,942 --> 00:55:21,318
How many rooms are there?

869
00:55:22,153 --> 00:55:25,197
Can I use one of your rooms as my office?

870
00:55:25,281 --> 00:55:26,741
-You need to behave.
-Have a seat.

871
00:55:27,491 --> 00:55:29,577
-Please have a seat.
-Thank you.

872
00:55:29,952 --> 00:55:32,830
I didn't have much time to prepare,
but I hope you enjoy.

873
00:55:33,372 --> 00:55:35,124
-Thank you.
-No problem.

874
00:55:35,666 --> 00:55:38,919
You know,
he hates inviting people to his house.

875
00:55:39,003 --> 00:55:41,213
-Do you know what he--
-Stop.

876
00:55:42,631 --> 00:55:46,260
I've changed a lot.

877
00:55:46,802 --> 00:55:48,637
People change.

878
00:55:48,721 --> 00:55:51,974
Of course, you do important work,
so it's natural for you to be prickly.

879
00:55:52,058 --> 00:55:53,392
If you're too easy-going,

880
00:55:53,476 --> 00:55:55,144
people don't take you seriously.

881
00:55:56,062 --> 00:55:57,730
-Ms. Cho.
-What?

882
00:55:57,813 --> 00:55:59,315
You're being so biased right now.

883
00:55:59,398 --> 00:56:01,108
Of course, I am biased.

884
00:56:02,401 --> 00:56:04,361
-Of course.
-Have some before it gets cold.

885
00:56:04,445 --> 00:56:06,030
Thank you.

886
00:56:09,658 --> 00:56:11,410
Move!

887
00:56:15,331 --> 00:56:16,165
Hey!

888
00:56:16,248 --> 00:56:20,377
Newly appointed CEO Yoon Yi-jun has begun
taking decisive steps to lead Taekang.

889
00:56:20,461 --> 00:56:23,380
He emphasized transparent management

890
00:56:23,464 --> 00:56:26,509
for a renewed management of the company.

891
00:56:26,801 --> 00:56:29,303
Taekang's brand reputation index

892
00:56:29,386 --> 00:56:32,598
has recently hit an all-time high.

893
00:56:32,681 --> 00:56:36,435
Why am I picking people up
when I'm already so busy?

894
00:56:36,894 --> 00:56:38,062
We're picking Jae-hee up.

895
00:56:38,145 --> 00:56:40,397
Exactly. Why am I being dragged along

896
00:56:40,481 --> 00:56:42,149
to pick up Detective Kang from work?

897
00:56:42,233 --> 00:56:45,486
Listen. The chairman position
at Taekang Cultural Foundation is vacant.

898
00:56:45,569 --> 00:56:46,487
So?

899
00:56:48,322 --> 00:56:50,491
I recommended someone.

900
00:56:51,826 --> 00:56:53,828
No, please. Tell me it's not true.

901
00:56:53,911 --> 00:56:55,329
Who did you recommend to whom?

902
00:56:55,412 --> 00:56:57,748
I recommended you to my father.

903
00:56:58,374 --> 00:57:00,960
So that's how it is,
Mr. Chairman of the foundation.

904
00:57:01,043 --> 00:57:04,380
Hey! I'm busy as it is!
I barely have time to go on dates!

905
00:57:04,463 --> 00:57:06,674
I just want to be your lawyer, Yi-jun.

906
00:57:07,424 --> 00:57:08,384
You're not listening.

907
00:57:12,221 --> 00:57:13,139
Watch it, man!

908
00:57:13,222 --> 00:57:15,141
Watch it!
I'm the chairman of a foundation!

909
00:57:29,238 --> 00:57:32,324
-She stepped on my car again.
-See you.

910
00:57:34,285 --> 00:57:36,704
When will you learn?

911
00:57:36,787 --> 00:57:38,372
Let go of me!

912
00:57:38,455 --> 00:57:39,456
Jae-hee!

913
00:57:41,584 --> 00:57:42,751
Would you look at him?

914
00:57:44,753 --> 00:57:48,883
When you finish mixing it up,
you add sesame oil.

915
00:57:49,091 --> 00:57:50,801
-How much?
-Two drizzles.

916
00:57:55,806 --> 00:57:56,807
Is it good?

917
00:57:57,892 --> 00:57:59,226
What? Is it bad?

918
00:58:01,061 --> 00:58:02,354
You didn't want it back then.

919
00:58:33,385 --> 00:58:38,390
Everyone. I'm finally
in the billionaire's secret room!

920
00:58:38,641 --> 00:58:42,895
Look! There's even a merry-go-round.

921
00:58:42,978 --> 00:58:45,064
I've never seen anyone
have this at home before.

922
00:58:45,147 --> 00:58:47,983
Look at that!
Are you seeing this, everyone?

923
00:58:48,067 --> 00:58:51,195
This is a limited edition.
Look how big this is!

924
00:58:51,278 --> 00:58:52,947
THAT THING IS HUGE
IS THIS A REAL ROOM?

925
00:58:53,030 --> 00:58:53,989
Come here.

926
00:58:54,073 --> 00:58:55,866
Please say hello.

927
00:58:56,200 --> 00:58:59,161
Hello. I'm Taekang's Yoon Yi-jun.
Nice to meet you all.

928
00:58:59,245 --> 00:59:01,914
Ara was
my daughter's favorite character too.

929
00:59:01,997 --> 00:59:03,707
What's next?

930
00:59:03,791 --> 00:59:06,293
I have another limited-edition item.

931
00:59:06,377 --> 00:59:09,672
For the subscribers
to my father-in-law's channel,

932
00:59:10,589 --> 00:59:13,342
I'd like to give each subscriber
one as a gift.

933
00:59:17,638 --> 00:59:20,474
I saw this place in my dream.

934
00:59:21,809 --> 00:59:24,728
You were in the dream.

935
00:59:25,521 --> 00:59:26,814
What kind of dream was it?

936
00:59:30,025 --> 00:59:31,110
A heart-fluttering one.

937
00:59:33,988 --> 00:59:38,075
Let's keep
giving each other butterflies for life.

938
00:59:40,035 --> 00:59:41,036
Okay.

939
00:59:49,086 --> 00:59:53,924
THANK YOU FOR WATCHING LOVE IN DISGUISE

940
00:59:54,008 --> 00:59:55,009
By the way,

941
00:59:57,177 --> 00:59:59,972
doesn't it feel like
someone is still watching us?

942
01:00:03,642 --> 01:00:06,520
Let's run on three.

943
01:00:09,523 --> 01:00:10,357
One.

944
01:00:10,941 --> 01:00:11,775
-Three.
-Three.

945
01:00:46,310 --> 01:00:48,187
SPECIAL THANKS TO CHOI HEE-JIN,
PARK JUN-MUYN, AND KIM SE-JEONG

946
01:01:09,625 --> 01:01:12,044
THANK YOU FOR GIVING ME
UNFORGETTABLE, PRECIOUS MEMORIES

947
01:01:12,127 --> 01:01:13,545
THANK YOU FOR ENJOYING THE SHOW

948
01:01:13,629 --> 01:01:15,923
I DON'T KNOW HOW TO SAY GOODBYE
SO I CAN'T LET IT GO

949
01:01:16,006 --> 01:01:17,549
KANG JAE-HEE BACK TO SERVICE!

950
01:01:17,633 --> 01:01:21,553
STAY WARM AND MAY GOOD FORTUNE
AND GRATITUDE ALWAYS BE WITH YOU

951
01:01:21,637 --> 01:01:25,557
THANK YOU FOR WATCHING THE SHOW

952
01:01:25,641 --> 01:01:28,560
THANK YOU FOR ENJOYING OUR SHOW

953
01:01:28,644 --> 01:01:31,563
I WAS HAPPY SHOOTING THE SHOW
I HOPE OUR HAPPINESS REACHES YOU

954
01:01:31,647 --> 01:01:34,566
WE WORKED HARD ON THIS SHOW
MAY IT BRING LAUGHTER AND COMFORT TO YOU

955
01:01:34,650 --> 01:01:37,569
THANK YOU FOR WATCHING THE SHOW

956
01:01:37,653 --> 01:01:40,572
LOVE IN DISGUISE!

957
01:01:40,656 --> 01:01:43,575
LOVE IN DISGUISE,
GUILTY OF STEALING THE VIEWERS' HEARTS

958
01:01:43,659 --> 01:01:46,578
THANK YOU FOR ENJOYING THE SHOW!

959
01:01:46,662 --> 01:01:49,581
WRAP UP THE YEAR WITH THIS SHOW!
PLEASE ENJOY THE SHOW

960
01:01:55,671 --> 01:01:58,549
I ENJOYED WORKING ON THE SHOW
THANK YOU FOR WATCHING UNTIL THE END

961
01:02:00,634 --> 01:02:03,637
Translated by Leo Chung
